  "summary": "This single-page letter, dated 30 March 1971, is from Indukumar C. Thakkar to M. R. Masani, President of the Swatantra Party. Thakkar thanks Masani for his appreciation and describes his decision to assist Swatantra Party candidates during the Rajkot election campaign as a duty arising from his role as a “Life Worker of the Party.”",
  "extent_caveat": false,
  "summary_structured": {
    "key_points": [
      "Thakkar acknowledges Masani’s letter of 22 March and thanks him for his appreciation.",
      "He says he had decided early in January to help Swatantra Party candidates in the election campaign.",
      "He travelled to Rajkot to assist Masani, describing the work as both a duty and a pleasure.",
      "He regrets that the voters of Rajkot District rejected Masani’s services.",
      "He expresses satisfaction at having fulfilled his duty and promises earlier and greater assistance in any future campaign.",
      "Thakkar’s wife joins him in thanking Masani and regrets that their efforts did not produce the success he deserved.",
      "The letter closes with best wishes for Masani’s future and an assurance of continued cooperation."
